<title>SWEDEN: SWIMMING-WORLD SHORT-COURSE CHAMPIONSHIPS MEDALS TABLE.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-WORLD SHORT-COURSE CHAMPIONSHIPS MEDALS TABLE.</headline>
<dateline>GOTHENBURG, Sweden 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Medals table at the</p>
<p>end of the first day of the four-day world short-course swimming</p>
<p>championsips:</p>
<p>		   Gold    Silver    Bronze</p>
<p> Australia	 3	  1	   2</p>
<p> China	     2	  1	   1</p>
<p> Sweden	    1	  1	   0</p>
<p> United States   1	  0	   2</p>
<p> Brazil	    1	  0	   0</p>
<p> Germany	   0	  2	   2</p>
<p> Japan	     0	  1	   0</p>
<p> New Zealand     0	  1	   0</p>
<p> Russia	    0	  1	   0</p>
<p> Britain	   0	  0	   1</p>
<p> Canada	    0	  0	   1</p>
<p>Note: Two bronze medals were awarded in the men's 400 metres</p>
<p>individual medley.</p>
</text>
